# Code Quality Principles

Follow DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself), KISS (Keep It Simple, Stupid), and YAGNI (You Aren't Gonna Need It) principles.

## Core Principles

### DRY: Reuse existing patterns and avoid code duplication
### KISS: Simplify code structure, inline simple one-liners
### YAGNI: Don't add functionality until needed

## Pattern Consistency
- Backend: Follow BaseAIService pattern for AI services
- Frontend: Use useStreamBase pattern for all hooks
- Extract hard-coded strings as constants
- Think holistically about related files that need updates

## Code Review Checklist
- [ ] Type safety with proper hints/annotations
- [ ] Proper error handling
- [ ] Naming conventions followed
- [ ] Correct directory placement
- [ ] Pattern consistency maintained
- [ ] No code duplication
- [ ] Simplicity over complexity
- [ ] Constants extracted
- [ ] Complex logic documented
